  "body": "## Scope\n\n`/os/workspace`: a user types what they need; Veklom compiles it into a bounded contract (ABIDE), shows one Action Review Card, and on approval requests a single-use grant, executes once, and reads the target back independently. The operator pages (Mount, Authority, Execute, Evidence) and the Consequence Ring read the same session storage, so this is a presentation of the same lifecycle through the same routes, not a second product.\n\nBase is `claude/cos-blueprint` (production is `cc8029d` on that branch; this builds on its tip `d85a85a`).\n\n## Commits\n\n**`725c99e` — task engine (pure, unit-tested)**\n- `lib/cos/tasks/task-reducer.ts`: every transition is caused by an observed ABIDE/CAPPO response or by the user's approval; no timers, clocks or randomness.\n  - Uncovered or blocked steps → `refused`, naming the exact clauses and which steps *are* covered.\n  - Lost execute answer → `outcome_unknown`; a later readback cannot upgrade it to Verified (reconciliation required).\n  - A recompile that changes the contract `canonical_hash` voids a prior approval.\n  - Readback compared with `compareReadback` (Verified / Degraded / Needs proof), the Execute page's rule.\n- `lib/cos/tasks/compile-shape.ts`: normalizes both shapes the ABIDE compile route answers with today (Blueprint contract, Govern plan). Never fills in fields the service did not return.\n- `lib/cos/tasks/pipeline-nodes.ts`: the five React Flow positions, status derived from task state only.\n- Stage registration (`stages.ts`, `nav.ts`, `maturity.ts` = Needs proof, `guides.ts`), nav icon.\n- `ConsequenceRing.tsx`: re-reads the session lease on `veklom.capability_lease.changed`.\n\n**`184e2bf` — page and components**\n- `TaskComposer`, `ConversationLog`, `ActionReviewCard` (steps + coverage; binding form when the covered step still needs its exact resource, ABIDE binds; one \"Approve and run once\" button), `PipelineCanvas` (via `GovernCanvas`), `TaskReceipt`, `ConversationWorkspace` (orchestration), `app/os/workspace/page.tsx` with the Consequence Ring on top.\n- **Honest labelling:** a governed-counter target is labelled *\"Sandbox pool: governed-counter test capability … not a Sarafu pool, a voucher, or a bank balance\"* next to the action and again on the receipt.\n- Mount reuses `mountRequestBody` with the bound intent (same request Authority sends). Execute uses the lease's token/nonce and presents `authority_epoch` when the grant stated one. Readback uses `targetStateReadbackPath`. Lease and consequence are written to the same session storage the operator pages read.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm run typecheck`: clean\n- `eslint` on changed files: 0 errors (repo-wide: 7 pre-existing warnings)\n- `npx jest lib/cos`: 67 passed (9 new)\n- `npm run build`: succeeds; route list includes `ƒ /os/workspace`\n- **Not verified against a running ABIDE or CAPPO.** I cannot reach either from this environment. The ABIDE response shape is taken from `app/os/govern/page.tsx` and `app/os/blueprint/page.tsx`; a raw compile response would let me pin the parser with a fixture.\n\n## How to test locally (for whoever has the Docker stack)\n\n1. Check out this branch, `npm ci`, run the dev server against the usual `.env` (ABIDE_URL, CAPPO, cAPI).\n2. Sign in with an account that has a bound workspace; open `/os/workspace`.\n3. Type `increment the counter` → expect a contract; if the step is unbound, enter resource `demo-counter` → Bind → \"Approve and run once\".\n4. Expected: grant `allow`, execute `allow` with receipt id, readback matching → badge **Verified**; `/os/execute` shows the same run.\n5. Type `order a pizza to 123 Main St` → expect `refused` with the clause named; nothing is approvable.\n6. Please paste the raw `POST /api/abide/v1/blueprint/compile` response body in a comment so the parser gets a fixture.\n\n## CI\n\n`update-release-draft` (Release Drafter) fails on this head as it does on every push to `main` since Oct 8; not this PR's (see comment). `ci-cd.yml` does not run on this base branch.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01V4sGzE1yp6kKZchCb4QpJN",
